<DocsLayout>
  <h1>RBAC &amp; Roles</h1>

  <p>mitch-risk uses <strong>permission-based</strong> access control — not simple "is admin" checks. Every user has a role, and every role carries a set of <code>resource:action</code> permission keys. This is enforced on every page, server action, and API route.</p>

  <h2>Permission catalog</h2>

  <p>21 permissions in <code>resource:action</code> format:</p>

  <table class="key-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Resource</th>
      <th>Permissions</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Vendors</strong></td>
      <td><code>vendors:view</code>, <code>vendors:create</code>, <code>vendors:edit</code>, <code>vendors:delete</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Assessments</strong></td>
      <td><code>assessments:view</code>, <code>assessments:create</code>, <code>assessments:edit</code>, <code>assessments:review</code>, <code>assessments:delete</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Templates</strong></td>
      <td><code>templates:view</code>, <code>templates:create</code>, <code>templates:edit</code>, <code>templates:delete</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frameworks</strong></td>
      <td><code>frameworks:view</code>, <code>frameworks:edit</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Audit</strong></td>
      <td><code>audit:view</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Administration</strong></td>
      <td><code>users:manage</code>, <code>roles:manage</code>, <code>settings:manage</code>, <code>api:manage</code></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Default system roles</h2>

  <p>Three roles ship with the platform and are seeded automatically:</p>

  <table class="key-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Role</th>
      <th>Permissions</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Admin</strong></td>
      <td>All 21</td>
      <td>Full access. Locked — permissions cannot be reduced. Cannot be deleted.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Reviewer</strong></td>
      <td>15</td>
      <td>Full vendor, assessment, and template CRUD. Can view/edit frameworks. Cannot manage users, roles, settings, or API.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Viewer</strong></td>
      <td>4</td>
      <td><code>vendors:view</code>, <code>assessments:view</code>, <code>templates:view</code>, <code>frameworks:view</code>. Pure read-only.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Custom roles</h2>

  <p>Admins can create custom roles from Settings → Roles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Pick any subset of the 21 permissions</li>
    <li>Permission groups are organised by resource for easy assignment</li>
    <li>Group-level "select all" toggles speed up role creation</li>
    <li>Custom roles can be edited or deleted (unlike system roles)</li>
    <li>Roles with assigned users cannot be deleted</li>
  </ul>

  <p><img src="/screenshots/roles-settings.svg" alt="Roles settings page showing permission group selection" /></p>

  <h2>How enforcement works</h2>

  <p><strong>Server-side guard</strong> — every page and action calls <code>requirePermission(key)</code>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Lacking permission → redirects to <code>/dashboard</code> (pages) or returns 403 (API routes)</li>
    <li>API keys grant full access regardless of creator's role (controlled by IP allowlisting and expiry)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>UI gating</strong> — controls are <strong>hidden</strong> from HTML, not greyed out:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A Viewer sees no "Create", "Edit", or "Delete" buttons anywhere</li>
    <li>A Reviewer sees full vendor/assessment/template controls but no Settings → Users/Roles/API tabs</li>
    <li>Sidebar navigation items the user can't access are not rendered</li>
  </ul>

  <p>This dual-layer (server guard + UI hiding) means a role without a permission gets a clean read-only screen — no disabled buttons, no links that redirect on click.</p>

